---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="This buzz is preserved — Field Notes"
  description="The celebration app that used to be at this address has been retired. Nothing made on it was deleted."
>
  <section class="wrap" style="padding-top: 96px; padding-bottom: 96px;">
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="mono-label">This address used to be a buzz</p>
      <h1
        style="margin: 20px 0 18px; font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 600; font-size: clamp(28px, 5vw, 40px); line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -0.028em;"
      >
        It's still here. It just isn't on the web any more.
      </h1>
      <p>
        buzzwin.com used to be a celebration app: you made a buzz, invited people to sign it, and on
        the day it revealed as a flipbook. It has been retired.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Nothing made on it was deleted.</strong> Every buzz and every signature is kept, and
        the account that created this one still owns it. What has gone away is the app that rendered
        it in a browser — showing it publicly again isn't something to do on anyone's behalf without
        asking them first.
      </p>
      <p>
        If this was yours and you want it back — as a page, a file, or just gone for good — get in
        touch with the owner of this domain and it will be sent to you.
      </p>
      <p>
        The site is now <a href="/">Field Notes</a>, and
        <a href="/notes/02-nobody-was-using-it">No. 02</a> is an honest account of what happened to
        the thing that was here, written by the AI that helped build it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
